</year>. Functional role of a conserved aspartate in the external mouth of voltage-gated potassium channels. <source>Biophys. J.</source> <volume>68</volume>:<fpage>1804</fpage>&#x02013;1813.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7612822</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Lagrutta, A.A., K.Z. Shen, A. Rivard, R.A. North, and J.P. Adelman. <year>1998</year>. Aromatic residues affecting permeation and gating in dSlo BK channels. <source>Pflugers Arch.</source> <volume>435</volume>:<fpage>731</fpage>&#x02013;739.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9479027</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Loboda, A., A. Melishchuk, and C. Armstrong. <year>2001</year>. Dilated and defunct k channels in the absence of k(+). <source>Biophys. J.</source> <volume>80</volume>:<fpage>2704</fpage>&#x02013;2714.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11371446</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Melishchuk, A., A. Loboda, and C.M. Armstrong. <year>1998</year>. Loss of <italic>shaker</italic> K channel conductance in 0 K<sup>+</sup> solutions: role of the voltage sensor. <source>Biophys. J.</source> <volume>75</volume>:<fpage>1828</fpage>&#x02013;1835.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9746524</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Molina, A., P. Ortega-Saenz, and J. Lopez-Barneo. <year>1998</year>. Pore mutations alter closing and opening kinetics in <italic>Shaker</italic> K<sup>+</sup> channels. <source>J. Physiol.</source> <volume>509</volume>(Pt 2):<fpage>327</fpage>&#x02013;337.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9575283</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Neyton, J., and C. Miller. <year>1988</year>. Discrete Ba<sup>2+</sup> as a probe of ion occupancy and pore structure in the high-conductance Ca<sup>2+</sup> activated K<sup>+</sup> channel. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>92</volume>:<fpage>569</fpage>&#x02013;586.<pub-id pub-id-type="p